<title>FRANCE: Lamassoure denies secret Franco-German agreement.</title>
<headline>Lamassoure denies secret Franco-German agreement.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French budget minister Alain Lamassoure denied on Wednesday evening that there was a secret Franco-German agreement to try and keep Italy and Spain out of the first wave of countries in the european monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no secret agreement between France and Germany on this subject,&quot; he told LCI television.</p>
<p>&quot;There is an agreement we have all signed and that is the Treaty of Maastricht. There are very precise and calculated conditions in the agreement that need to be fulfilled,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope that Italy and Spain will be part of it, but they will have to meet the criteria,&quot; Lamassoure said.</p>
</text>
